%I A401493 #10 Nov 03 2026 17:02:17
%S A401493 1,2,4,11,30,109,406,1864,8169,36897,158351,671656,2657424,11481042,
%T A401493 46683483,190658218,789399022
%N A401493 Number of unlabeled Riordan graphs on n vertices.
%C A401493 A Riordan graph of order n is a simple graph on the vertices 1..n whose adjacency matrix A satisfies A(i,j) = [t^(i-2)] g(t)*f(t)^(j-1) mod 2 for i > j, for some power series g, f over GF(2) with f(0) = 0. Equivalently, the strictly lower triangular part of A is the binary Riordan matrix (g,f) of order n-1 (Cheon, Jung, Kitaev and Mojallal, 2019).
%C A401493 a(n) is the number of isomorphism classes of graphs on n vertices that admit at least one Riordan labeling. Determining this number is Problem 2 of Cheon et al.
%C A401493 The number of labeled Riordan graphs of order n is (4^(n-1)+2)/3 = A047849(n-1).
%H A401493 Gi-Sang Cheon, Ji-Hwan Jung, Sergey Kitaev and Seyed Ahmad Mojallal, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.laa.2019.05.033">Riordan graphs I: Structural properties</a>, Linear Algebra Appl. 579 (2019), 89-135.
%H A401493 Arnauld Mesinga Mwafise, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23676628">riordan-graph-enumerator</a>, C++ software for enumerating, listing and sampling Riordan graphs, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A401493 a(n) <= A000088(n).
%F A401493 a(n) <= A047849(n-1).
%e A401493 a(4) = 11: every graph on 4 vertices is a Riordan graph.
%e A401493 a(5) = 30: of the 34 graphs on 5 vertices, exactly 4 are not Riordan graphs: C_4 + K_1, K_4 + K_1, and the complements of the chair and of K_{1,3} + K_1 (here + denotes disjoint union).
%Y A401493 Cf. A000088, A047849, A401495, A401496.
%K A401493 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401493 1,2
%A A401493 _Arnauld Mesinga Mwafise_, Oct 27 2026
